--- !u!114 &70513225
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 70513224}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: caf16c3cf9779a448bf8015237a39bfb, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::BigDialogueTrigger
  bigDialogue: {fileID: 6822750942231247413, guid: 06efdedda4c78d742a7532094a922827, type: 3}
  boxCollider: {fileID: 70513226}
  player: {fileID: 0}
  triggered: 0
  lines:
  - (Okay, time to finally get through to him)
  - Dad, we need to have a talk, now.
  - Yes, we do. Your behavior yesterday was unacceptable. I think you-
  - No.
  - Excuse me? How dare you-
  - Stop. I'm not gonna let you interrupt me.
  - You're finally gonna listen to me.
  - ................
  - Look, I get that Mom's death was brutal for us, I really do. There are days when
    I don't want to get out of bed.
  - But grief is not an excuse to treat others around you like scum.
  - Think about it, when was the last time we had a conversation that didn't end
    with you hurling insults my way?
  - Do you really think yelling at me everyday is gonna make things better?
  - And your drinking problem! What the hell is that all about? That's certainly
    not gonna make things better!
  - I always come home to a house full of empty beer bottles! That stuff deeply saddens
    me.
  - Are you trying to get alcohol poisoning? If you die from that, what do you think
    will happen to me?
  - I lost Mom already. I really, REALLY, don't want to lose you, too.
  - So please...
  - ...please...
  - ...................................
  - '*sniff*'
  - D-dad?
  - Y-you're right... you're so right... What the hell am I doing?
  - I've allowed myself to get swallowed by my own grief, and I couldn't see any
    of the problems I've been causing.
  - I can't believe it... I've treated you so harshly this past half year... I-
  - I'M SO SORRY!!!!!
  - Dad...
  - It's time... to fix all the problems I've caused.
  - My daughter... I know I've been an absolutely terrible dad recently, but...
  - Could you please give me a chance to make things right?
  - Dad! Of course! We'll get through this together!
  - Thank you so much. Let's get back to how things were.
  changes: 00000101010100010100000000000000000001000101000000010100000101
  talker: 1
  react: 1
  emotionChanges: 00000000020000000000000003000000010000000300000003000000020000000200000003000000030000000300000003000000030000000300000003000000030000000200000000000000040000000400000004000000040000000400000004000000020000000400000004000000050000000500000005000000
